{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>וְהָיָה כְשִׁבְתּוֹ עַל כִּסֵּא מַמְלַכְתּוֹ.</b> Rashi explained: if he does thus, it is fitting that his kingship be established. There is a hint to this matter: כס״א is an acrostic for כֶּסֶף סוּס אִשָּׁה — in the merit that he will be careful regarding all three of these, he will merit to sit upon the throne of HaShem, as it is written (I Chronicles 29:23): ״וַיֵּשֶׁב שְׁלֹמֹה עַל כִּסֵּא ה׳״. And therefore he must beware of those things that remove his heart from HaShem and separate between himself and HaShem, for multiplying silver and gold brings him to forgetfulness of HaShem, as it is written (Deuteronomy 8:13–14): ״וְכֶסֶף וְזָהָב יִרְבֶּה לָּךְ וְגוֹ׳ וְרָם לְבָבֶךָ וְשָׁכַחְתָּ אֶת ה׳״. And likewise, multiplying horses is a cause to remove his trust from HaShem so that he trusts in horse and chariot, as it is written (Isaiah 31:1): ״הוֹי הַיֹּרְדִים מִצְרַיִם לְעֶזְרָה וְעַל סוּסִים יִשָּׁעֵנוּ״. And this is what it says: ״וְלֹא יָשִׁיב אֶת הָעָם מִצְרַיְמָה לְמַעַן הַרְבּוֹת סוּס״. The prohibition is not about going to Egypt for trade; rather, the essence of the prohibition is because multiplying horses removes his trust in HaShem from him. Therefore He commanded that he not return the people to Egypt in order to multiply horses, as though all his trust were in horse and chariot — but for other merchandise it is permitted to go to Egypt. And this reasoning is more precious than what all the commentators said about this. And likewise, multiplying wives causes the turning of his heart from HaShem, as happened to Solomon." "And He said, <b>וְכָתַב לוֹ אֶת מִשְׁנֵה הַתּוֹרָה הַזֹּאת וְגוֹ׳.</b> In order that he read in it and know to beware of these three. Corresponding to multiplying silver He said: ״לְבִלְתִּי רוּם לְבָבוֹ מֵאֶחָיו״, for silver brings haughtiness of heart; and corresponding to multiplying wives He said: ״לְבִלְתִּי סוּר מִן הַמִּצְוָה יָמִין וּשְׂמֹאל״, in the manner stated above: ״וְלֹא יַרְבֶּה לּוֹ נָשִׁים וְלֹא יָסוּר לְבָבוֹ״; and corresponding to multiplying horses He said: ״לְמַעַן יַאֲרִיךְ יָמִים עַל מַמְלַכְתּוֹ הוּא וּבָנָיו בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — to say that if he trusts in horse and chariot, he will die in battle, for a horse is a false hope for salvation, and in the abundance of his might he will not deliver his soul. But if he trusts in the salvation of HaShem, he will live long and not die." "And He said, <b>בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל.</b> To say that one who trusts in horse and chariot seeks salvation and help from the lands of the nations and not בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל, in the manner stated (Isaiah 31:1): ״הוֹי הַיּוֹרְדִים מִצְרַיְמָה לְעֶזְרָה״ וְגוֹ׳. But if he does not multiply horses for himself, then he will find salvation בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל, and not from the lands of the nations. And he hinted further that Israel is saved by HaShem who walks בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל, as it is written (Deuteronomy 23:15): ״כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ מִתְהַלֵּךְ בְּקֶרֶב מַחֲנֶיךָ״ — meaning, he will live long, etc., from Him who is בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {2 "The final phrase of comment 2, מִמִּי שֶׁהוּא בְּקֶרֶב יִשְׂרָאֵל ('from Him who is in the midst of Israel'), is syntactically compressed; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:58.841289198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}